   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_02"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Why do songs get stuck in my head? I've had the same jingle for three days.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 0.33,
   "block": "music.dlg6",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "They're called earworms. Usually it's a catchy, simple bit of melody that your brain keeps replaying because it feels unfinished.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.31,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "music.dlg6"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Any way to make it stop?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.61,
   "block": "music.dlg6",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Oddly, listening to the whole song all the way through can help. It gives your brain the ending it wants.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 1.06,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "music.dlg6"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "It's a jingle for",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 1.48,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "music.dlg6"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "a carpet shop, there's no whole song.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 2.85,
   "block": "music.dlg6",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Ah. Then try chewing gum, it really does help some people. Or do a puzzle that keeps your mind busy.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 1.07,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "music.dlg6"
  },
  {
